# CVE-2024-21413 — My Practical Learning Journey

## Room Overview

I worked through the TryHackMe room covering **CVE-2024-21413**, a Microsoft Outlook vulnerability involving specially crafted Moniker Links.

The practical exercise demonstrated how a malicious email could cause a vulnerable Outlook client to interact with a remote SMB resource, resulting in an **NTLM authentication exchange** that could be observed by an attacker-controlled listener in the lab.

Although I was able to complete the practical, I initially had difficulty understanding how the individual components were connected. The main challenge was not running the commands, but understanding **which machine was doing what, why different IP addresses were required, and how the authentication flow worked**.

This write-up documents what I learned from the practical, including the mistakes and confusion I encountered.

---

