# 11. Understanding the Captured Authentication Data

The lab demonstrated the capture of **netNTLMv2 authentication data**.

This does not mean that the victim's plaintext password was simply transmitted across the network.

Instead, Windows uses a **challenge-response authentication process**.

Simplified:

```text
Victim
   ↓
Receives authentication challenge
   ↓
Calculates authentication response
   ↓
Sends response
   ↓
Remote listener observes the exchange
```

The captured authentication material can potentially be subjected to password-guessing attacks in an authorized environment, but it is not equivalent to receiving the user's plaintext password.

This distinction helped me connect this room with the NTLM concepts I had studied earlier.

